   "text": "Specialized silicon just got a brutal customer test.\n\nThe Tech Buzz reports that Etched, an AI chip startup building ASICs optimized for transformer models, doubled its valuation to $21 billion in a month after Jane Street became the first customer to deploy its specialized AI cluster and then led a new funding round. The bet is familiar: general-purpose GPUs can do everything, while a chip tuned for one architecture can run that workload faster and cheaper. Jane Street\u2019s deployment is framed as an early real-world proof point in the search for Nvidia alternatives.\n\nThat pattern matters outside the chip race too. Products that feel simple to end users usually rest on infrastructure that has ",
